SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Sept 24 thru 30**\nUpcoming **music e
 vents** may be found here:\n[https://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/](htt
 ps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/)\n\n**Assorted entertainment\, festi
 val & market events may be found here:**\n[https://visithendersonvillenc.o
 rg/calendar-of-events](https://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of-event
 s)\n\n**Library programs** may be found here:\n[https://hendersonpl.libcal
 .com/](https://hendersonpl.libcal.com/)\n\n**Library After Hours**\nSeptem
 ber 25 @ 5:30 pm - 7:00 pm\; Free\nJoin for an evening of crafts\, library
  behind the scenes tour\, and a personalized book recommendations panel in
  an evening tailored for adults in the community!\nHenderson County Main L
 ibrary\; 301 N Washington Street\, Hendersonville\nhttps://visithendersonv
 illenc.org/event/library-after-hours\n\nFriday\, September 25\nKaraoke and
  dancing with DJ Fr3sh\n7-11pm\, Sissy’s Farm\, 3016 Chimney Rock Road\,
  Hendersonville\n\n**Saturday\, September 26**\n16th Annual Hendersonville
  **Oktoberfest at Southern Appalachian Brewery**\nNoon-6:30pm\, Southern A
 ppalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n\n**Art on M
 ain**\n**September 26&27** @ 10:00 am - 5:00 pm\nArt on Main is a juried a
 nd judged fine art and fine craft show which brings 100+ high quality loca
 l and regional artist vendors to Hendersonville\, and attracts thousands o
 f art loving visitors.\n\nBritish & European Automobile & Motorcycle Show\
 n**September 26\;** 9:00 am - 2:30 pm\n25th Annual Autumn in the Mountains
  British and European Automobile and Motorcycle Show\n[Hosted by the Briti
 sh Car Club of Western North Carolina](https://visithendersonvillenc.org/e
 vent/autumn-in-the-mountains-british-european-automobile-motorcycle-show)\
 nSaturday\, September 26\nTuxedo Junction Band\n6-9pm\, J&M Farm\, 3016 Ch
 imney Rock Road\, Hendersonville\n\n**Henderson County Curb Market Ol’ T
 imey Day**\n**Sat\; Sept 26** @ 8:00 am - 2:00 pm\; Free\nHighlights are e
 xpected to include antique cars\, traditional craft and skill demonstratio
 ns\, live cider pressing\, fresh ice cream made using an antique tractor e
 ngine\, outdoor games\, kid-friendly activities\, and local food.\nhttps:/
 /visithendersonvillenc.org/event/henderson-county-curb-market-ol-timey-day
 \n\nSaturday\, **September 26**\n**The Showboat Band**\n6-9pm\, Bold Rock 
 Hard Cidery\, 72 School House Rd\, Mills RiverFor Sept 17 thru\n\n**Sunday
 \, September 27**\nSunday/Funday with **Peggy Ratusz & Friends**\n4-6pm\, 
 Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n\nSunday\, 
 September 27\nHendersonville Ballroom Dance Club Tea Dance - Attire: Fall 
 Colors\n2:30-6pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhodes Veterans Center\, 900 North 
 Main St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\nDoors open at 2:30pm and dance lesson w
 ill start on time. 3-3:45pm – Night Club 2 dance lesson with Barbara Fin
 n. 3:45-6pm - Open Ballroom Dance to the music of DJ Gary Bills. Ample par
 king at the front entry of the building\, take the elevator or stairs to t
 he upper level. Parking is limited at the rear entrance\, both front and b
 ack doors will be unlocked. Our dances are open to the public and everyone
  is invited. Enjoy Ballroom Dancing to dance tunes including Swing (East &
  West Coast)\, Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. There is also 
 a dance mixer. Cost: $5 per person at door.\n\nWednesday\, September 30\nJ
 ason DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (Each Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalach
 ian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n\n***Thursday\, October 1\, 
 2026***\n***Movie Matinee- Pressure\; 2 PM***\nIn the tense 72 hours befor
 e D-Day\, General Dwight D. Eisenhower and Captain James Stagg face an imp
 ossible choice- launch the most dangerous seaborne invasion in history or 
 risk losing the war altogether.\n**Hendersonville Main Library**\nhttps://
 hendersonpl.libcal.com/\nhttps://hendersonpl.libcal.com/event/14834310\n\n
 Pumpkin Palooza at The Nix Pumpkin Patch\n**October 3** @ 11:00 am - 4:00 
 pm\; Free\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/pumpkin-palooza-at-the-
 nix-pumpkin-patch\n\nThese are NOT hosted events and are posted for inform
 ational purposes only. Please make personal arrangements to meetup with fr
 iends and family.\nIf you wish to attend and host one of these events\, I 
 will post the event as an individual happening. Hosting only requires bein
 g focal point for others and making introductions. Simple!!
