SUMMARY:Cataloochee ELK (GSMNP)
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**Note: WAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS 
 DRIVERS SIGN ON.**\nI am going to Cataloochee Valley in the Smoky Mtn Nat'
 l Pk to explore\, picnic and\, hopefully\, **catch the Elk during their 'r
 ut' bugling.** Up to 16 are welcome to join me.\nThis event is suitable fo
 r non-hikers and “grade school-age” grandchildren.\n**Since the storm 
 destroyed much of the valley road\, we will park near the church and see h
 ow far we can walk into the valley.**\nThe elk usually overnight in the va
 lley. Usually\, by 4-5pm. There is never a guarantee. But\, if we get luck
 y\, it's an event not to be missed.\nCataloochee Valley has a historical h
 ome\, church and barn which we will take time to explore.\n**The plan is t
 o arrive early afternoon to give time to explore and 'PICNIC' before the e
 lk 'present' themselves.**\nBring a folding chair\, bug spray\, camera\, w
 ater & food.\nHiking NOT required.\n**We are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: 
 “We will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real
 ’ hike groups don’t !!**\n**[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUf
 DY](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bsh_8qxUfDY)**\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL
  BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\n**I currently have 2.5 driver(s). (=10 ppl)
 **\nTHOSE WHO MIGHT WISH TO DO THIS ‘ON THEIR OWN’ MAY CONTACT ME\, vi
 a email (see below)\, FOR EXACT DIRECTIONS. (mid Sep thru-Mid Oct).\nDrive
  time: 1.25 hr/55 mi (one way) Via I-40W to exit 20 (Jonathan Creek) **(SM
 OKY MTN NATL PK PARKING TAGS REQR’D – I WILL CONTACT DRIVERS WITH THE 
 INFO).**\n**\\*\\*Special Note\\*\\*:** The last 5 miles of the drive are 
 not suitable for low sedans. It is a switchback climb up a mountain gravel
  road. Those with excessive fear of height or prone to carsickness will be
  uncomfortable on this road.\nGoogle Maps: = “Cataloochee Valley – Elk
  Watching”\nGoogle Maps: = “Palmer Chapel Methodist Church”\n**Retur
 n Not earlier than: 7:30 PM**\n**CARPOOL CONTRIBUTIONS APPRECIATED. $7.00 
 SUGGESTED**\n**DOGS: Since this in in the Smoky Mtn Nat'l Pk\; dogs are NO
 T invited to this event.**\nWeather Check: Jonathan Creek\, NC\nIncessant 
 prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair.\nWe suggest slightly ope
 n windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so judge 
 accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of others.\
 nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes in
 to the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nAll hikes are at your own ris
 k. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver
 : There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participa
 nt\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability
  the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and membe
 rs for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occu
 r while participating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle d
 uring this trip. Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules and
  regulations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\,
  and not to become intentionally separated from the group. The leader(s) a
 lso has the right to use any images collected on this trip for recording o
 n website photo collections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\
 n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: [https://ww
 w.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums](https://www.flickr.com/photos/14
 6993931@N05/albums)**
